nected San Francisco with both Marin County and the East Bay. A fleet of six historic…"],["Maritime Museum","sight",37.8064,-122.4239,"","10AM-4PM daily","","","","r","Shaped like a ship, this historic building was built by the WPA as a bathhouse and served as the Maritime Museum for many years before a renovation. Inside you'll find maritime exhibits and beautiful underwater-themed murals."],["Aquatic Park and Municipal Pier","sight",37.8068,-122.4229,"","","","","","r","A great place to take a break from the bustle of Fisherman's Wharf. There is a small beach at the foot of the park where you'll see kayakers, kite fliers, and swimmers from the nearby swim clubs. At the end of the park is Municipal Pier…"],["San Francisco Segway Tours - Electric Tour Company","activity",37.8062,-122.4211,"Tours depart from the rear parking lot at 757 Beach St","Segway tours daily 9AM, 12:30PM and 4PM April–October & 10AM and 1:30PM November–March","","","","r","Take a 2½-hour tour of Fisherman's Wharf on a segway"],["McCormick and Kuleto's Seafood Restaurant","restaurant",37.8062,-122.4228,"Ghirardelli Square, 900 North Point St","Mon-Thu 11:30AM-10PM, Fri Sat 11:30AM-11PM, Sun 10:30AM-10PM","","","","r","A good seafood restaurant that also serves other fare such as pastas and steaks. The restaurant is perched atop Ghirardelli Square and has magnificent views of the bay, as well as a spacious and airy feel inside."],["Buena Vista Cafe","bar",37.8065,-122.4207,"2765 Hyde St","Mon-Fri 9AM-2AM, Sat Sun 8AM-2AM","","","","r","Famous for its Irish Coffee, supposedly the first to serve it in America, and great views over the bay."],["Ghirardelli Choclaterie and Cafe","bar",37.8057,-122.4223,"Ghirardelli Square","Mon-Thu 8:30AM-8PM, Fri 8:30AM-10PM, Sat 9AM-10PM, Sun 9AM-8PM","","","","r","Serving premium espresso drinks, pastries, and desserts."],["Wave Organ","sight",37.8086,-122.44,"at the end of Yacht Rd","It's best at high-tide &mdash; 5:30AM","","","","r","Designed by George Gonzales and Peter Richards in 1986, the Wave Organ is a system of PVC pipes that harness the power of the ocean to create music... or at least what can be interpreted as music! There is a unique space at the end of a…"],["The Long Now Foundation","sight",37.8068,-122.4307,"Landmark Building A","","","","","r","The Long Now Foundation runs a steampunk style bar called 'The Interval' with some exhibits related to their work to promote long-term thinking."],["Museo ItaloAmericano","sight",37.8068,-122.4314,"Fort Mason Center, Building C","Tue-Sun noon-4PM, Mon by appointment","","","","r","Hosts photo exhibits and the work of modern Italian artists."],["BATS Improv at Bayfront Theater","activity",37.8067,-122.4318,"Fort Mason Center, Bldg B, 3rd floor","Shows usually start at 7PM/8PM","","","","r","BATS is a performing arts theater company that focuses on all forms of improvisational format, including theatersports. They also provide classes for anyone interested."],["Blue Bear Performance Hall","activity",37.8066,-122.4307,"Fort Mason Center, Bldg D, 2nd floor","","","","","r","The Blue Bear Performance Hall is used mostly for school musical performances. They have a music school that teaches all kind of music from Jazz to rock-n-roll to musicians of all ages. The hall also hosts some independent stage…"],["Cowell Theater","activity",37.8088,-122.4315,"Fort Mason Center, Middle Pier","See website for schedule and times","","","","r","Hosts theater, dance, talks, and film festival productions among other things."],["Magic Theatre","activity",37.807,-122.4308,"Fort Mason Center, Bldg D, 3rd floor","Wed–Sat 8PM, Sun 2:30PM and 7PM","","","","r","The Magic Theater is where you can go if you are interested in seeing productions from new and established American playwrights such as the Pulitzer Prize-winner, Sam Shepard."],["Young Performers Theatre","activity",37.8066,-122.4314,"Fort Mason Center, Bldg C, 3rd floor","Sat 1PM, Sun 1PM and 3:30PM. Shows do not run every week, see website for exact dates","","","","r","The Young Performers Theatre is a professional children's theater. It hosts a dozen or so shows each year and also offers classes in the dramatic arts, creative drama, comedy and musical theater."],["Ace Wasabi's Rock-N-Roll Sushi","restaurant",37.8001,-122.438,"3339 Steiner St","Mon-Thu 5:30PM-10:30PM, Fri-Sat 5:30PM-11PM, Sun 5PM-10PM","","","","r","This sushi place is popular with the locals, offering good sushi with a rock and roll theme. Quirky and a bit of fun."],["Alegrias","restaurant",37.8002,-122.4348,"2018 Lombard St","Wed-Mon 5:30PM-10PM","","","","r","Alegrias is a colorful, friendly, and romantic little Tapas bar in the Marina. Like many other Tapas bars, it's a great place to go if you want to sample many flavors and tastes from small plates. If you're still hungry after that, they…"],["Dragon Well Restaurant","restaurant",37.8007,-122.4386,"2142 Chestnut St","11:30AM-10PM daily","","","","r","Light but satisfying modern Chinese food &mdash; not your typical oily dishes here!"],["Bobo's","restaurant",37.8014,-122.4257,"1450 Lombard St","Sun-Thu 5PM-10PM, Fri-Sat 5PM-11PM","","","","r","Popular steakhouse in the Marina, Bobo's is a \"surf-n-turfers\" dream. The menu boasts excellent steaks (porterhouse, fillet mignon, New York bone-in) combined with mussels, shrimp, lobster, and Dungeness crab... yummy! Bobo's is a…"],["Izzy's Steaks & Chops","restaurant",37.8002,-122.4381,"3345 Steiner St","Sun-Thu 5PM-10PM, Fri-Sat 5:30-10:30PM","","","","r","Classic steak restaurant with wood floors, saw dust, comfortable booths, steak sauces, and the requisite cowboy hat to boot! Their pricing is affordable and their steaks big and tasty."]]}